---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import { links } from '../data/site'
---
<SiteLayout title="Community" path="community" description="Nova community links and the current absence of chat platforms.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">No invented channels</span>
      <h1>Find the project.</h1>
      <p>The repository is the source of truth. No Discord, forum, mailing list or social account is claimed because none has been verified as official.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 20px;">
    <div class="wrap grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon">↗</div>
        <h3>GitHub</h3>
        <p>Issues, discussions and release assets live in the repository when a public remote is configured. This deployment may use a placeholder GitHub URL until then.</p>
        <div style="margin-top: 16px;"><a class="button" href={links.github} rel="noreferrer">Open GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon">◆</div>
        <h3>Contributor path</h3>
        <p>Read the contributing guide, run the compiler and website checks, then pick an evidence gap. Keep changes reviewable and document limitations.</p>
        <div style="margin-top: 16px;"><a class="button" href="../contribute/">Contributing →</a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="notice"><strong>Security reports:</strong> do not post secrets or exploits publicly. Use the repository's private advisory channel when available. See <a href="../security/">Security</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
